IQ-TREE 2.0.7 built Apr  1 2024

Input file name: exp_trim.aln
Type of analysis: tree reconstruction + ultrafast bootstrap (1000 replicates)
Random seed number: 1

REFERENCES
----------

To cite IQ-TREE please use:

Bui Quang Minh, Heiko A. Schmidt, Olga Chernomor, Dominik Schrempf,
Michael D. Woodhams, Arndt von Haeseler, and Robert Lanfear (2020)
IQ-TREE 2: New models and efficient methods for phylogenetic inference
in the genomic era. Mol. Biol. Evol., in press.
https://doi.org/10.1093/molbev/msaa015

Since you used site-specific frequency model please also cite: 

Huai-Chun Wang, Edward Susko, Bui Quang Minh, and Andrew J. Roger (2018)
Modeling site heterogeneity with posterior mean site frequency profiles
accelerates accurate phylogenomic estimation. Syst. Biol., 67:216–235.
https://doi.org/10.1093/sysbio/syx068

Since you used ultrafast bootstrap (UFBoot) please also cite: 

Diep Thi Hoang, Olga Chernomor, Arndt von Haeseler, Bui Quang Minh,
and Le Sy Vinh (2018) UFBoot2: Improving the ultrafast bootstrap
approximation. Mol. Biol. Evol., 35:518–522.
https://doi.org/10.1093/molbev/msx281

SEQUENCE ALIGNMENT
------------------

Input data: 187 sequences with 340 amino-acid sites
Number of constant sites: 7 (= 2.05882% of all sites)
Number of invariant (constant or ambiguous constant) sites: 7 (= 2.05882% of all sites)
Number of parsimony informative sites: 321
Number of distinct site patterns: 340

SUBSTITUTION PROCESS
--------------------

Model of substitution: LG+SSF+F+G4

State frequencies: (site specific frequencies)

Model of rate heterogeneity: Gamma with 4 categories
Gamma shape alpha: 1.0867

 Category  Relative_rate  Proportion
  1         0.1539         0.2500
  2         0.5014         0.2500
  3         1.0130         0.2500
  4         2.3317         0.2500
Relative rates are computed as MEAN of the portion of the Gamma distribution falling in the category.

